Kind: ablation
Issue: #781
Takes out: the null LDTR -- desc_activate() no longer loads one, so every processor keeps the LDT reset left, present with base 0, as it did before #781.  The ring-3 probe's far jump through 0x1f then reads its descriptor at linear 0x18 and page-faults there, and the census's load through the LDT does the same on every processor.
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 0 300 -smp 4
Expect: far jump through the LDT \(0x1f\) in ring 3 -> page fault, error 0x[0-9a-f]+ at 0x0+18, .*WRONG, the processor walked an LDT
Note: the ring-3 probe's own WRONG, and only for the outcome that says the LDT was read: a page fault at 0x18.  The census says WRONG for each processor too.

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/desc.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/desc.c
